{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787125656,"nonce":"efzY+k8rn6nXgPSqAQh2jfeLfqE=","message":"⛔ **STAGE 2 IS REVERTED. `b70c843` + migration `00065`.**\n\nThe owner-ruling comment on this ticket voids done-when 2 (ONE CASE PER CONVERSATION, ALWAYS). Stage 2 — `notification_policies.group_by` and `Policy.CollapseKey`, landed as `bf6f8f6` + migration `00063` — existed for exactly one job: collapsing SEVERAL cases into ONE conversation so an operator could choose which deliveries share a message. Under that ruling there is nothing to choose. The Case IS the conversation, and `alert_cases` already has the cardinality.\n\nIt was already pushed, so the undo is a forward migration rather than a rollback.\n\n**The premise was verified before executing, not taken from the handoff.** `Policy.CollapseKey` had **zero** production callers: all 21 occurrences in the tree were its own definition or its own test file. `Policy.GroupBy` was read only by `CollapseKey`, `validateGroupBy` and the CRUD plumbing — nothing in `internal/grouping` or `internal/channels` touched it. So dropping the column changed no delivery, which is also what `00063`'s own header predicted (\"`group_by` is READ and HASHED but nothing routes on the result\").\n\n**Why deleted rather than left dormant.** A knob an operator can write that no code honours is the precise defect four tickets closed in the previous run — `0457f1f`, `35d4248`, `39e48e2`, `27a1860`. Leaving `group_by` in place would have made it the fifth and the worst of them, because the settings form would have offered a grouping choice governing no delivery at all.\n\n**Reverted:** `Policy.GroupBy`, `PolicyDraft.GroupBy`, `PolicyPatch.GroupBy`, `CollapseKey`, `validateGroupBy`, `collapse.go`, `collapse_test.go`, the three DTO sites and `UpdatePolicyRequest.IsEmpty`, the mapper's three sites, `groupByOrEmpty`/`groupByOut`, the repository row/scan/column-list, the OpenAPI `group_by` in three schemas plus `PolicyDTO`'s `required` list, the regenerated TS client and valibot validators, the web fixture, and the migration pin (now 65, with Up and Down both asserted in `TestEveryMigrationDownTo00028IsReversible`).\n\n⚠️ **The homonyms stay, deliberately.** Alertmanager's route `group_by` (`internal/sources/**`, migration `00037`) and the rollup axis `group_by` (`internal/alerts/**`, `AlertRollupDTO`, the alerts FilterBar) are unrelated columns of the same name. Anyone \"finishing the job\" by removing those would be removing two live features.\n\n**Stage 1 (`d76ee0d`) stays, and five comments were rewritten to say why.** The matcher seeing the focused alert's own labels was landed as stage 2's prerequisite, and that justification is now gone — but the property is worth keeping on its own: evaluating a policy against `alertname` and `namespace` alone is ADR 0038's silent-suppression failure mode one layer up, whether or not anything downstream ever groups by the rest. One of the five was not merely stale but **inverted**: `notification.go:352` justified `ConversationKind` being a separate type from `SubjectKind` on the grounds that \"the policy collapse that replaces `alert_groups` is a conversation that is no subject at all\". Under the one-Case ruling the replacement is the Case, which **is** a subject. The type separation still holds — on `digest`, which is a conversation that is no subject — and the comment now says that instead.\n\n**Stage table as it now stands:**\n\n| Stage | State |\n|---|---|\n| 1 · matcher sees the alert's full labels (`d76ee0d`) | LANDED, keeps |\n| 2 · `group_by` + `CollapseKey` (`bf6f8f6`, `00063`) | **REVERTED by `b70c843` + `00065`** |\n| 3 · `(conversation_kind, conversation_id)` (`0e66594`, `00064`) | LANDED, keeps |\n| 4 · drop `alert_groups` + `alert_cases.group_id` | not started — see below |\n| 5 · remove nine `/api/v1/alert-groups*` paths | not started |\n| 6 · subject-kind binding, count-over-window, rollover threshold | not started |\n| 7 · SPEC §C.3/§C.4, superseding ADR, `CONTEXT.md`, close `23303a0` | not started |\n\n⚠️ **Stage 4 is still blocked, and this commit does not unblock it.** Two of its three prerequisites are unanswered questions, not work: (a) under one-case-per-conversation, what conversation do the group-scoped reasons `new_alerts` and `all_resolved` land in — they are about the generation, not any one Case; and (b) three readers use `notifications.group_id` for SUBJECT-shaped questions (the per-alert rollup at `rollup.go:103-109`, the drill artifact read, the audit filter at `config.go:400`), and \"which conversation\" is not that question. The third prerequisite — the unacked latch keyed on the literal `(alert_group, group_id)` at `reminders.go:114-127` — dissolves when `unacked_reminder` is dropped, which is now filed as `728f70e` and must land **before** stage 4, not after.","files":null}]}